[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HCT (Bartel)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=7,557): skew = -0.188, excess kurtosis = 1.664, D'Agostino K^2 p = 3.97e-72, Jarque-Bera p = 1.27e-199
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.381, excess kurtosis = 2.271, D'Agostino K^2 p = 7.13e-126, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 180.567, p = 9.25e-14
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 7.182, p = 0.000765
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
